vaporOS NuttX patch: sim-usrsock-event-loop

Problem:   With CONFIG_SIM_NETUSRSOCK the simulator's sockets connect and send, but a
           receive never completes: recv() waits for ever, poll() never reports
           POLLIN, a blocking connect() cannot finish. The host sockets' readiness is
           turned into usrsock events by host_usrsock_loop(), and nothing calls it.
Evidence:  Commit bbcf8fe30b "usrsock: used wd timer to process loop event" removed the
           host_usrsock_loop() call from sim_loop_task() and added sim_usrsock_work(),
           but that function only re-queues itself. A TCP client against a host
           python http.server: the request arrives and is answered, the reply is
           never seen by the NuttX side (40 retries over 10 s).
Fix:       Call host_usrsock_loop() from sim_usrsock_work().
Upstream:  YES. It is a regression in a recent upstream commit; the fix is one line.

Apply: git -C ../nuttx apply ../vaporOS/patches/nuttx/sim-usrsock-event-loop.patch   (setup.sh does this)

diff --git a/arch/sim/src/sim/sim_usrsock.c b/arch/sim/src/sim/sim_usrsock.c
index c8210d0336..ae41fc663b 100644
--- a/arch/sim/src/sim/sim_usrsock.c
+++ b/arch/sim/src/sim/sim_usrsock.c
@@ -415,6 +415,7 @@ static const usrsock_handler_t g_usrsock_handler[] =
 
 static void sim_usrsock_work(void *arg)
 {
+  host_usrsock_loop();
   work_queue_next_wq(g_work_queue, &g_usrsock.work, sim_usrsock_work,
                      NULL, SIM_USRSOCK_PERIOD);
 }
